@section('content')<section class="section narrow"><div class="eyebrow">FAQ</div><h1>How the platform works</h1><div class="faq"><details open><summary>Are rates calculated in the browser?</summary><p>No. The browser submits the requested pair and amount to Laravel. The server obtains the configured market rate and creates a time-limited quote.</p></details><details><summary>Does creating an order move funds automatically?</summary><p>Not by itself. The delivered architecture records the order lifecycle and payment data. Production payment processors, wallet infrastructure, blockchain nodes and payout credentials must be configured and verified before real-money processing is enabled.</p></details><details><summary>Where is the database?</summary><p>The production configuration is designed for Supabase PostgreSQL. Database credentials belong in Vercel environment variables.</p></details><details><summary>Can I deploy this to Vercel?</summary><p>Yes. The package includes a Vercel-oriented Docker configuration for Laravel. Set all production environment variables in Vercel before opening the service to customers.</p></details></div></section>@endsection
